    [41108] = "Every Khaz Algar delve on Tier 4 or higher with lives left, as a tank. Only the role at the end seems to count.",
    [41092] = "Catch the new battle pets of Undermine and Gutterville (the new area in the Ringing Deeps). The Spring-Loaded Ribbitron only shows up as a backline pet in Undermine battles; if one pet won't appear, battle random pets there until it does.",
    [41542] = "The Undermine elite pets and tamers with aquatic pets only. The tamer whose parrot transforms into a robot is the toughest; start with a frog that can kiss and water-jet.",
    [41548] = "The Undermine elite pets and tamers with magic pets only. If a win doesn't count, log out and in, or try on another character.",
    [41169] = "Max renown with the Council of Dornogal, the Assembly of the Deeps, the Hallowfall Arathi and the Severed Threads.",
    [41350] = "Exalted with Darkfuse Solutions. Undermine weeklies, S.C.R.A.P. jobs and chests give reputation; it's a long grind, so stack any reputation bonus you can.",
    [41351] = "Revered with all four Undermine cartels. Your chosen cartel each week gains the most, so rotate between them.",
    [41352] = "Exalted with all four Undermine cartels. Rotate your weekly cartel choice so each one reaches Exalted.",
    [40874] = "Max reputation with the Weaver in Azj-Kahet. Choosing their pact speeds it up.",
    [40875] = "Max reputation with the General in Azj-Kahet. Choosing their pact speeds it up.",
    [40876] = "Max reputation with the Vizier in Azj-Kahet. Choosing their pact speeds it up.",
    [40636] = "The optional Azj-Kahet storylines. Unlike the other zones, some of these need the zone's campaign finished on the character doing them.",
    [40822] = "Fly over every area of Azj-Kahet. The Crawling Chasm is the one players most often miss; its posted coordinates lead into rock, so search the caves around it. The Umbral Bazaar is in the City of Threads.",
    [40840] = "Ten of the listed Azj-Kahet rares and special encounters. Some sit in the City of Threads or the lower caves. Players report the Kaheti Bladeguard criterion is credited by a different enemy, so if it won't tick, kill the others nearby.",
    [40851] = "Ten of the listed Hallowfall rares and special encounters. One patrols, so look around its marked spot.",
    [40702] = "Every skyriding glyph in Khaz Algar for the reward mount. Each zone's glyph achievement lists its glyphs with places.",
    [40631] = "Finish one Tier 1 delve.",
    [40725] = "Reach level 80 and finish the main Khaz Algar story on your warband.",
    [41209] = "Four Battle for Azeroth appearance achievements. The quickest are a season's PvP honor set and raid sets from solo LFR wings.",
    -- raids (more)
    -- Manaforge Omega (Normal or harder)
    [41613] = "Loom'ithar: before the pull, every player types /cuddle or /cower at the boss. It doesn't matter who picks what; the boss only gets a small buff from the majority.",
    [41614] = "Soulbinder Naazindhri: kill every Little Unbound Soul during the fight. They have little health, so burst them when they appear.",
    [41615] = "Forgeweaver Araz: keep the second Arcane Echo alive, have its tank drag it through the arcane beam in the intermission, then through void orbs in phase 2 until it turns void-forged, and kill it. If no echo is empowered by 25%, reset.",
    [41616] = "The Soul Hunters: the blindfold lies near the tents on the right of the boss room. Every player uses it at least once during the fight (you only see the bosses for a minute).",
    [41617] = "Fractillus: the hardest of the set. The fight runs to the enrage while walls fill the room; bring many healers and focus everything on wall placement.",
    [41618] = "Nexus-King Salhadaar: reveal the hidden assassin at the far end of the bridge on the left, past the boss platform, and talk to her; she helps in the fight.",
    [41619] = "Dimensius: every raid member must be hit by Reverse Gravity. Stand in the circles around the targeted players so everyone gets knocked up. Needs at least 10 players.",
    [42118] = "Plexus Sentinel: in each of the three run-back intermissions, mice spawn along the corridor (mostly at the sides and back). Every player runs over one and gets a debuff; dying afterwards is fine.",
    -- Liberation of Undermine (more)
    [41694] = "Cauldron of Carnage: talk to the fan NPC outside the arena to become Flarendo's fan, then kill Torq's lieutenant first. Keep the buff until the kill; a wipe removes it.",
    [41695] = "Cauldron of Carnage: talk to the fan NPC outside the arena to become Torq's fan, then kill Flarendo's lieutenant first. Keep the buff until the kill; a wipe removes it.",
    [41711] = "Sprocketmonger Lockenstock: don't get hit by any of the listed abilities. Dying without having been hit still counts.",
    -- Undermine and K'aresh odd jobs
    [41626] = "C.H.E.T.T. lists come from the machine on the second floor of the Incontinental Hotel (right of the stairs) from Cartels of Undermine renown 13. Finish four of the listed tasks and hand it in.",
    [41627] = "Hand in two C.H.E.T.T. lists. You get one list a week; extra ones cost Undermine currency.",
    [41629] = "Hand in 100 C.H.E.T.T. lists (or earn Employee of the Month). Plan for a long time: one free list a week.",
    [41708] = "Five rats to pick up in Undermine: under the stands on a dumpster, on a trash can one floor up, on a railing, in a burrow and by a fake palm tree.",
    [41778] = "Win the two challenging races in the Oasis in K'aresh. They come from a quest that rotates with the twice-weekly reset.",
    [41809] = "One repeatable quest for each Oasis species. They rotate with the weekly and mid-week resets, so each is only up for a few days.",
    [41811] = "Raise every Oasis species to full integration with the campaign and the repeatable quests. If a species was maxed before a hotfix, do one more of its quests to get credit.",
    [41812] = "The Oasis questline in K'aresh; parts are weekly gated. Anything available shows on the map, so do everything in the Oasis each week.",
    [41978] = "Two K'aresh warrants. The warrant keys can be bought on the Auction House.",
    [41979] = "Four K'aresh warrants. The warrant keys can be bought on the Auction House.",
    [41980] = "Every K'aresh warrant. The keys can be bought on the Auction House; the mount arrives by mail.",
    [41998] = "Ten incursion quests: the three blue daily quests from the Hallowfall incursion quest giver. Alts can do them too, so ten can be done in one day.",
    [42730] = "The Ethereal Voidforged Container in the Ruins of Yaathron needs the Reshii Wraps' What Lies Beyond power and K'aresh Trust renown 11. Glide down onto it from the high ground.",
    [42738] = "Two swords in the untethered space of K'aresh. You need the What Lies Beyond power on the Reshii Wraps to see them.",
    [61017] = "Phase-Lost weapons drop at random (about one orb in five) from Phase Diving orbs. You need Reshii Wraps rank 3; orbs are spread over all of K'aresh and each orb serves one player.",
    [42316] = "Buy the Manaforge armor set; the cloak needs Loombeast Silk (Loom'ithar, once a week per account) and Manaforge Vandals renown 2, sold by the vendor outside the raid.",
    [42800] = "Buy and equip a full season 3 honor armor set from the PvP vendor in Dornogal. Every piece must be equipped (no longer refundable).",
    [41714] = "Five Gob-Trotter schematics from the delve vendor in Dornogal, unlocked by your warband's season 2 delve journey progress.",
    [42678] = "Five Mana-Skimmer cosmetics from the delve vendor in Dornogal. If Energy Thrusters won't count, learn the other thruster schematic too.",
    [42740] = "Fly over every area of K'aresh. Vanquisher's Wake is the floating island at the top of the map.",
    [41119] = "Liberation of Undermine, One-Armed Bandit: pick up one of the four casino chips in the casino area before his room and put it in its slot machine outside the room, then kill him. Red (fire rings to dodge) is the easiest.",
    [41122] = "One-Armed Bandit with all four chips in their machines: fire rings, healing reduction, silences and extra boss health together. Much easier with high item level and an extra healer.",
    [41208] = "Vexie and the Geargrinders: steer a bike into each of the five objects around the arena (dumpster, trash pile, tire stack, tool rack, storage crate) once, then kill the boss. Keep removing the boss's plating as usual.",
    [41211] = "Mug'Zee: before pulling, the raid stacks next to the purple casino chip in the Gallagio (don't click it) and waits for the fountain splash to dye everyone the same colour. The dye lasts 20 minutes; nobody may die before the kill.",
    [41337] = "Mug'Zee: free the murloc stuck at the bottom of the aquarium on the way in and talk to him before the pull. During the fight, sleepy fish land in bubbles: pop the bubble, stand on the fish and /sleep. Every raid member needs it once.",
    [41338] = "Rik Reverb: during the Hype Hustle intermission, one player at each side of the arena /dances at the disco ball until it lights up.",
    [41347] = "Chrome King Gallywix: in one intermission (not the first, when only one platform is open) detonate Giga Bombs at three different Giga Controls. Assign three bomb carriers and walk in together.",
    [41554] = "Cauldron of Carnage: buy both punch potions from the vendors before the boss and drink both during the fight (they share a one-minute cooldown). You personally need the combined Hubris buff on the kill.",
    [41596] = "Stix Bunkjunker: every time he throws out garbage, roll over or burn all of it before the next wave (he gains an Impressed buff when it's all gone). Burning trash hurts, so bring extra healing.",
    [41590] = "S.C.R.A.P. jobs: talk to the job NPC, then shovel trash piles to fill the bar in two minutes. Blue circles double your speed, green ones knock you back; put out fires, click mines and break trash bags. A paid robot helps.",
    [41591] = "25 S.C.R.A.P. jobs in Undermine. The job location rotates; see Cleanin' the Streets for all seven sites.",
    [41592] = "50 S.C.R.A.P. jobs in Undermine.",
    [41593] = "A S.C.R.A.P. job at every one of the seven sites in Undermine. Only one site is active at a time, so check back as it rotates.",
    [41214] = "Both Worldsoul Memories in Undermine. They don't show while you're on a Shipping and Handling contract: clock out in your car first.",
    [41589] = "Kick the cans lying around Undermine. Two always sit together in the south; the rest spawn at the marked spots.",
    [41595] = "Buy a full honor or forged armor set from the PvP vendor in Dornogal, including the cloak that belongs to your class's set.",
    [40730] = "The Silken Court in Nerub-ar Palace: before the bosses, pick up the Box of Candy (on the railing at the foot of the left stairs) and the Anub'arash plushie (at the door to the Ky'veza path). Throw the plushie at Anub'arash and the candy at Takazj, then pull without entering combat first; if you do, they respawn after a minute or two.",
}

